From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 May 2021 09:16:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Update unit formating in QT to be 10^8 and Lotus properly
 (#182)

The QT Wallet uses completely different formatters from the rest of
the codebase and was missed during the previous re-denomination patch.
This commit changes the QT wallet to use the 10^6 base unit, and ensures
the QT wallet uses the appropriate formats.

Rebase provenance: this historical change was adapted onto the pinned
Bitcoin ABC base. Source diff is the recorded Lotus V1 replay commit below.

Historical-source-commit: 4cd2f286b0f484fbc79b73ca0137942fb18d2b5c
Recorded-replay-commit: 267afcd25c5ae49a6b3cf6b703aaa4871735ce61

diff --git a/src/qt/bitcoinunits.cpp b/src/qt/bitcoinunits.cpp
index 0c12779968..4229b5c551 100644
--- a/src/qt/bitcoinunits.cpp
+++ b/src/qt/bitcoinunits.cpp
@@ -37,10 +37,18 @@ static const unitNameMap bchUnits = {
         {"Satoshi (sat)",
         "Satoshi (sat) (1 / 100" THIN_SP_UTF8 "000" THIN_SP_UTF8 "000)"}},
 };
+static const unitNameMap lotusUnits = {
+    {BitcoinUnits::Unit::base,
+        {"XPI",
+        "Lotus"}},
+    {BitcoinUnits::Unit::sub,
+        {"Satoshi (sat)",
+        "Satoshi (sat) (1 / 100" THIN_SP_UTF8 "000)"}},
+};
 // clang-format on
 
 static const unitNameMap &getUnitsAtRuntime() {
-    return gArgs.GetBoolArg("-ecash", DEFAULT_ECASH) ? xecUnits : bchUnits;
+    return gArgs.GetBoolArg("-ecash", DEFAULT_ECASH) ? xecUnits : lotusUnits;
 }
 
 BitcoinUnits::BitcoinUnits(QObject *parent)
diff --git a/src/qt/test/wallettests.cpp b/src/qt/test/wallettests.cpp
index 0601f1a28d..2cf38fbad6 100644
--- a/src/qt/test/wallettests.cpp
+++ b/src/qt/test/wallettests.cpp
